# Midfoot relationships in 3D reasoning practice

Six original formative concepts add twelve exact left/right targets: the three
cuneiforms and the first, second and fourth metatarsals. These bones already have
text quick checks. This batch adds them to the actual whole-body/regional 3D
reasoning engine, its existing feedback/retry flow and revision-bound Review
worksheet. Existing questions are not rewritten or remapped.

The new prompts contrast usual midfoot articulations and AP/oblique radiographic
alignment landmarks. They select existing whole source bones; no ligament,
articular surface, fracture, new segmentation, radiograph or patient study is
created. A static reference mesh does not establish patient alignment, ligament
integrity, diagnostic thresholds or spatial CT/MRI registration. All content is
draft pending the owner's source/revision-bound radiologist review.

## Evidence and commercial-use boundary

Facts were checked on 23 October 2026 against primary educational institutions:

- [Texas Tech lower-limb bones](https://anatomy.ttuhscep.edu/anatomytables/bones_lowerlimb.html): cuneiform positions and proximal navicular articulation.
- [AO Surgery Reference](https://surgeryreference.aofoundation.org/orthopedic-trauma/adult-trauma/midfoot/lisfranc-injury/treatment-of-lisfranc-injuries): second metatarsal/middle-cuneiform relationship and medial-cuneiform/second-metatarsal interval.
- [POSNA foot-dislocation study guide](https://posna.org/physician-education/study-guide/foot-dislocations-(lisfranc-and-subtalar)): recessed second metatarsal base and AP/oblique alignment landmarks. Its pediatric injury-management recommendations are not imported or generalized to adult treatment.

These are factual references, not imported anatomy datasets or permissions to
reproduce publisher material. No external text passage, question, diagram,
texture, font or image is copied or bundled. The prose is newly authored and no
new dependency, model or paid service is introduced. Existing retained BodyParts3D
source licensing, notices and holds remain unchanged.

`scripts/pin-midfoot-relationships-reasoning.mjs` reproduces complete identities
from the trusted displayed catalogue at parent source
`66ac064579ee23c5739d0907e8378e0e2d57d7bd`. Runtime matching compares every
identity field, source hash and side, not merely a label or FMA identifier.
Choices remain eligible same-side source selections and honor loaded bundles and
current scope. A changed question changes teaching-review evidence; no approval
is inherited from a text quiz or another source revision.

Run `npm run midfoot-relationships-reasoning:test` after regenerating the original
renderer and display-pin outputs. Source tests do not prove GPU, acquired-study,
signed-in Website, assistive-technology, clinical or release acceptance. Website
source integration is separate and this candidate is not installed into the
owner's unchanged local preview.
